       The robustness attribute specifies the behavior of the mutex  when  the
       owning  thread  dies without unlocking the mutex.  The following values
       are valid for _r_o_b_u_s_t_n_e_s_s:

       PPTTHHRREEAADD__MMUUTTEEXX__SSTTAALLLLEEDD
              This is the default value for a mutex attributes object.   If  a
              mutex  is  initialized  with the PPTTHHRREEAADD__MMUUTTEEXX__SSTTAALLLLEEDD attribute
              and its owner dies  without  unlocking  it,  the  mutex  remains
              locked  afterwards  and  any future attempts to call pptthhrreeaadd__mmuu‐‐
              tteexx__lloocckk(3) on the mutex will block indefinitely.

       PPTTHHRREEAADD__MMUUTTEEXX__RROOBBUUSSTT
              If a mutex is  initialized  with  the  PPTTHHRREEAADD__MMUUTTEEXX__RROOBBUUSSTT  at‐
              tribute  and its owner dies without unlocking it, any future at‐
              tempts to call pptthhrreeaadd__mmuutteexx__lloocckk(3) on this mutex will  succeed
              and  return  EEOOWWNNEERRDDEEAADD  to  indicate that the original owner no
              longer exists and the mutex is in an inconsistent  state.   Usu‐
              ally  after  EEOOWWNNEERRDDEEAADD  is returned, the next owner should call
              pptthhrreeaadd__mmuutteexx__ccoonnssiisstteenntt(3) on the acquired  mutex  to  make  it
              consistent again before using it any further.

              If  the  next  owner  unlocks  the mutex using pptthhrreeaadd__mmuutteexx__uunn‐‐
              lloocckk(3) before making it consistent, the mutex  will  be  perma‐
              nently  unusable  and  any  subsequent attempts to lock it using
              pptthhrreeaadd__mmuutteexx__lloocckk(3) will fail with the error  EENNOOTTRREECCOOVVEERRAABBLLEE.
              The  only  permitted  operation  on  such a mutex is pptthhrreeaadd__mmuu‐‐
              tteexx__ddeessttrrooyy(3).

              If the next owner terminates before  calling  pptthhrreeaadd__mmuutteexx__ccoonn‐‐
              ssiisstteenntt(3), further pptthhrreeaadd__mmuutteexx__lloocckk(3) operations on this mu‐
              tex will still return EEOOWWNNEERRDDEEAADD.

